89367.270555   ALWAYS ASKS YOU FIRST
89367.270557     bash     Run one command line through bash — really bash, including on Windows, where it is Git Bash.
89367.270559     (and any network request, per host, every time)
89367.270560 
89367.270561   MAY ACT WITHOUT ASKING
89367.270562     ask      Put a question to the user and wait.
89367.270563     edit     Change ONE snippet inside an existing file, leaving the rest untouched.
89367.270564     glob     List the files under a directory, by name.
89367.270565     grep     Search the CONTENTS of files under a directory with a regular expression, line by line.
89367.270567     read     Read a file in the workspace by workspace-relative `path`, OR a fetched document by `ref` (the id `web` returns).
89367.270568     recall   Search Marlowe's own memory: what the user said in earlier sessions, and what Marlowe has learned.
89367.270569     remember Ask the harness to record something worth keeping.
89367.270570     run      Delegate a sub-task to a child run and wait for it.
89367.270571     use      Find and load a skill.
89367.270572     web      Fetch one URL over https and return the page.
89367.270573     write    Create a file, or replace all of its contents.
89367.270574     Whether these ask depends on the trust tier this run was granted. The trust ledger that would raise a tier does not exist yet, so today they run at the tier the profile starts with.
89367.270575 
